# Cloudflare Workers static-asset upload exclusions (gitignore-style
# syntax). The assets directory is the repo root ("."), so everything
# here that isn't a genuine site asset must be excluded, or Wrangler
# tries to upload it as a public file.
#
# The specific failure this was added to fix: `npx wrangler deploy`
# reinstalls Wrangler itself (and its own local runtime dependency,
# `workerd`, a ~144 MB binary) into node_modules/ as part of running the
# deploy command -- which then gets swept up as a "site asset" purely
# because it happens to sit inside the assets directory at deploy time,
# not because it's anything to do with the actual website. Deleting
# node_modules in the *build* command doesn't help, since the *deploy*
# command recreates it afterward; excluding it here is the fix Wrangler
# itself is designed for.

node_modules/
.git/
.github/
.wrangler/
cloudflare-worker/
scripts/
tests/
docs/
